[2026-01-14T19:30:36.316514] Smith-Waterman matrix fill has diagonal dependencies: H[i][j] depends on H[i-1][j-1], H[i-1][j], H[i][j-1]. Cannot parallelize arbitrary cells.

Key observations:
1. ConstructMatrix: Wavefront/antidiagonal parallelization is the standard approach - cells on same antidiagonal are independent
2. FindHighestScore: trivially parallelizable (reduction over rows)
3. Traceback: inherently sequential (follows path back)

Chosen strategy: Antidiagonal wavefront
- Partition each antidiagonal k into independent cells
- Process antidiagonals sequentially, cells within parallel
- Deterministic: fixed worker pool, fixed partition per antidiagonal

Rejected alternatives:
- Row-parallel: violates deps (H[i][j] needs H[i-1][j])
- Block tiling: complex, >250 LOC likely, needs synchronization barriers
- SIMD vectorization: Go has limited SIMD, doesn't match CPU-bound worker model

Bounded patch: 1 file (smith_waterman.go), ~100 LOC changes

